摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH Skills Nexus — 从安装、版本管理到跨机器、跨 Agent 协同，DSH 技能全生命周期管理 · Full lifecycle management for DSH skills","id":"gh:1342631584","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-skills-nexus","slug":"xiaxi626/dsh-skills-nexus","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","import","plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH Skills Nexus — 从安装、版本管理到跨机器、跨 Agent 协同，DSH 技能全生命周期管理 · Full lifecycle management for DSH skills"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-skills-nexus"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"⭐ **If this project helps you, welcome to Star for support!**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"DSH skill lifecycle manager — from git repo cloning, external directory linking, package import/expo"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"rt, to group management, health checks, and cross-machine transport. Keeps up with the latest DSH ve"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"rsion, compatible with the official filesystem provider."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"dsh-skills-nexus is a community-maintained DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin, not an official DeepSeek A"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"-nexus is a community-maintained DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin, not an official DeepSeek AI product."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Capabilities"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Direction | What you get | Entry point |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Git-backed installs | Any `SKILL.md` repo from any git host, pinned to a branch, tag or commit; co"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"llection repos install one subdirectory with partial clone + sparse checkout; wrapper detection runs"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" before registering | `add` |\n| Version management | Refresh branch-tracked clones, preview remote c"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"hanges without a checkout, move a clone to another ref, undo the last version change | `update` / `d"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"iff` / `switch-version` / `rollback` |\n| External references | Register skills that already live in "},{"id":"p9s6","text":"another agent's directory — no clone, no copy, no writes there | `link` / `remove --group` |\n| Proje"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"ct-scope skills | View any project folder's skills (parsed names/descriptions), link directories int"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"o `<project>/.dsh/skills` (the root the provider scans first), enable/disable/remove links, report d"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"angling ones; no manifest, clone or copy | `--project` |\n| Cross-machine transport | Package entries"},{"id":"p9s10","text":" with their provenance, rebuild them elsewhere (optionally at the exact recorded commit), give a fro"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"zen entry its git source back | `export` / `import` / `adopt` |\n| Grouping and toggles | Group by so"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"urce or a custom L1 name; enable or disable one entry or a whole group prefix | `enable` / `disable`"},{"id":"p9s13","text":" / `--group` |\n| Health and cleanup | Read-only checkup of the manifest, links and clones, with an o"},{"id":"p9s14","text":"ptional remote update check; purge accumulated artifacts | `doctor` / `purge` |\n| Automation | Versi"},{"id":"p9s15","text":"on-1 JSON reports on stdout, stable exit codes, name-only listing | `--json` / `list --names` |\n| We"},{"id":"p9s16","text":"b panel | Browse entry cards, preview and link a local source, run the health check, adopt a source-"},{"id":"p9s17","text":"less entry, search and filter | panel |\n| Shell completion | Generated completion script for bash, z"},{"id":"p9s18","text":"sh, fish or PowerShell | `completions` |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"`dsh plugin --profile <name> add \"github:owner/repo\"` forwards to pnpm, and\n**only packages with `ds"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"h.bundle.patch` are activated as profile layers**. A\ncontent repo with just `SKILL.md` + `references"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"/` + `scripts/` has no Cordis\nwrapper, so this path doesn't work. `dsh-skills-nexus` fills the gap:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| command | installs | requires `dsh.bundle.patch`? |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| `dsh plugin add github:owner/dsh-skills-nexus` | nexus itself (once) | yes |\n| `dsh-skills-nexus a"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"dd github:owner/any-skill` | pure SKILL.md content repo | **no** |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"> **Not sure which command fits your repo?** Read\n> **nexus vs `dsh plugin` — when to use which**.\n>"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" Short version: repo has `SKILL.md` → nexus; repo is a pure plugin\n> (`cordis.patch.yml` / `dsh.bund"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"le.patch`, no `SKILL.md`) → `dsh plugin`;\n> has both → your choice (nexus = content, plugin = code)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Install nexus"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Optional: register as a DSH plugin"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"To register nexus in the DSH `web` profile, run the following (replace `web`\nif you use a different "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"er nexus in the DSH `web` profile, run the following (replace `web`\nif you use a different profile):"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"In a **web** session this adds the Skills Nexus settings panel\nalong with its `/skills-nexus/*` HTTP"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" routes; in non-web hosts the layer stays\ndormant. It still **does not provide a global CLI command "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"and is not a\nprerequisite for the CLI install below** — skip it if you only need the CLI\nto manage s"},{"id":"p19s4","text":" not a\nprerequisite for the CLI install below** — skip it if you only need the CLI\nto manage skills."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Install the CLI globally"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Install the CLI globally — **this** is what puts the `dsh-skills-nexus` command\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Notes & limitations"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"- **`add` then visibility**: with the default configuration the official\nfilesystem provider watches"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" the skills root, so newly added skills appear\nin new conversations of an already-running host withi"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"n its stability\nwindow — no reload needed. Hosts running without the watcher pick changes\nup on the "},{"id":"p23s4","text":"next rescan/restart; the web panel flags this with a \"next host\nstart\" notice.\n- **Version pinning &"},{"id":"p23s5","text":" updates**: pin a ref with `#branch`, `#tag`, or\n`#commit-sha`. At install time the manifest records"},{"id":"p23s6","text":" the exact resolved\ncommit (`commit`) — a lightweight lock that `list` shows. `update` only\nfast-for"},{"id":"p23s7","text":"wards **branch**-pinned skills (printing the commit change);\n**tag/commit**-pinned skills are fixed "},{"id":"p23s8","text":"points: it verifies the checkout\nstill matches the pin (and restores it if it drifted) instead of pu"},{"id":"p23s9","text":"lling, so\na pinned version never silently drifts. When no `#ref` is given, the CLI\ndetects the remot"},{"id":"p23s10","text":"e's default branch via `git ls-remote --symref` (falls back\nto `main`).\n- **Skill content repos only"},{"id":"p23s11","text":"**: this is *not* a replacement for `dsh plugin add`\nof real Cordis plugins. If a repo already ships"},{"id":"p23s12","text":" a `dsh.bundle.patch`, install\nit the normal way — nexus is for repos that don't. See\nnexus vs `dsh "},{"id":"p23s13","text":"plugin` for the full decision guide.\n- **External entries (`link` channel)**: `link trae-cn` / `link"},{"id":"p23s14","text":" trae` / `link qoder` / `link qoder-cn` / `link codebuddy` / `link workbuddy` creates *external* ent"},{"id":"p23s15","text":"ries\nthat symlink to directories you already own (`~/.trae-cn/skills/`, `~/.trae/skills/`, `~/.codeb"},{"id":"p23s16","text":"uddy/skills/`,\n`~/.workbuddy/skills/`, or the user-level and marketplace-plugin skill directories un"},{"id":"p23s17","text":"der `~/.qoder` and `~/.qoder-cn`). Nexus\nnever clones, updates or deletes those directories — `remov"},{"id":"p23s18","text":"e` only deletes the\nlink and the manifest entry. External entries carry a `groupPath` (e.g.\n`['trae-"},{"id":"p23s19","text":"cn', 'skills', 'brainstorming']`) for hierarchical grouping; `enable`\nand `disable` accept `--group "},{"id":"p23s20","text":"<path>` to batch-toggle every entry under a\nprefix. The web panel renders grouped entries under coll"},{"id":"p23s21","text":"apsible L1 group\nheaders with a group-level Switch.\n- **Project scope**: `link` / `list` / `enable` "},{"id":"p23s22","text":"/ `disable` /\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
